One crucial limitation: No Ghidra checklist can guarantee that you will find every bug-bounty vulnerability. Some vulnerabilities exist only in backend code, runtime behavior, application configuration or business logic.

For Android bug bounty, I recommend using JADX and Ghidra together: JADX for Java/Kotlin, Ghidra for native code.

My suggested next step is to build a Ghidra automated security-analysis workflow that searches native APK libraries for these categories, groups the results by vulnerability type, and produces a report containing function names, addresses and cross-references.
